1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,833
Causal attention must not read future values.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,233
This nntrainer test shows that it does.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:09,033
With zero logits and values 2, 10, 50,

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,967
the outputs should be 2 and 6.

5
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:13,467
Both are about 20.67 instead.

6
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:16,900
Changing the final value changes earlier outputs.

7
00:00:17,067 --> 00:00:18,867
A causal mask must prevent that.

8
00:00:19,433 --> 00:00:22,000
A square mask fails on rectangular scores.

9
00:00:22,167 --> 00:00:25,700
A finite penalty and later chunks also leak future values.

10
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:28,933
The patch sets forbidden scores to negative infinity

11
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,600
and respects the query offset.

12
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:35,067
Twenty-one tests fail before the patch. All forty-two pass after.

13
00:00:35,233 --> 00:00:40,300
Native CPU, float32. Key cases repeat in three fresh processes.

14
00:00:40,867 --> 00:00:43,733
Reported upstream. Maintainer review is pending.

15
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:47,267
Attention engineers: reproduce it at gero.uz.
